\begin_layout Standard
Prove Step 5 in the proof of Theorem 21.
 That is, 
\begin_inset Formula $u$
\end_inset

 constructed in the proof is unique up to positive affine linear transformation,
 i.e., if there is another function 
\begin_inset Formula $v:Z\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$
\end_inset

 such that 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

 is represented by the function 
\begin_inset Formula $E_{\pi}v$
\end_inset

, then there are real numbers 
\begin_inset Formula $a$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $b$
\end_inset

 such that 
\begin_inset Formula $a>0$
\end_inset

 and for each 
\begin_inset Formula $z\in Z,u(z)=av(z)+b$
\end_inset

 .
