\begin_inset Formula $E_{\pi}u$
\end_inset

 representes the preferences 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

, it must be that 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi\sim\lambda_{\pi}\overline{\pi}+(1-\lambda_{\pi})\underline{\pi}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
But if so, then since 
\begin_inset Formula $E_{\pi}u$
\end_inset

 is also linear and represents these same preferences, we have
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $E_{\pi}u=E_{\lambda_{\pi}\overline{\pi}+(1-\lambda_{\pi})\underline{\pi}}u$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset


\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $=\lambda_{\pi}E_{\overline{\pi}}u+(1-\lambda_{\pi})E_{\underline{\pi}}u$
\end_inset


\end_layout

